{
  "dom_id": "question-134229",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "After Rocky ate his part of the adult dog food, the remaining amount of adult dog food is$\\,$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,$than the remaining amount of puppy food because $3\\,\\frac{3}{4}$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $\\frac{11}{7}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Leonard has $3\\,\\frac{3}{4}\\,\\text{kg}$ of adult dog food and  $\\frac{11}{7}\\,\\text{kg}$ of puppy dog food remaining.\n\nWe cannot compare the fractions directly as they don't have a common denominator.\n\nWe can make a common denominator of $4\\times 7=28.$\n\nTo put $3\\,\\frac{3}{4}$ over a denominator of $28,$ we first convert to an improper fraction and then multiply the numerator and denominator by $7:$\n\n$$\n3\\,\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{15}{4}=\\frac{15\\times 7}{4\\times 7}=\\frac{105}{28}\n$$\n\nTo put $\\frac{11}{7}$ over a denominator of $28,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{11}{7}=\\frac{11\\times 4}{7\\times 4}=\\frac{44}{28}\n$$\n\nWe can now compare the fractions $\\frac{105}{28}$ and $\\frac{44}{28}$ by looking at the numerators only.\n\nSince $105>44,$ the correct statement must be:\n\n$$\n\\frac{105}{28}>\\frac{44}{28}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is\n\n\"After Rocky ate his part of the adult dog food, the remaining amount of adult dog food is $>$than the remaining amount of puppy dog food because $3\\,\\frac{3}{4}>\\frac{11}{7}.$\"",
